cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the engineering report, please cite it as below."
title: "Qwen3.8-Flash-Next Heterogeneous Engine: resident-state stochastic computation on a two-accelerator appliance"
type: software
date-released: 2026-09-07
version: 0.1.0-rc1
abstract: >-
  Engineering record of a two-accelerator (4x MI50 gfx906 + NVIDIA GB10) heterogeneous
  native-inference appliance and a GPU-native stochastic evaluation engine that treats a
  language model's resident causal state as a conditioned transition operator: fork, deterministic
  counter-based RNG, field advance with pruning and compaction, weighted statistical reduction,
  Monte Carlo validation against analytic integrals, variance reduction, stochastic rendering,
  and a model-backed conditioned stochastic field.
keywords:
  - heterogeneous inference
  - stochastic computation
  - Monte Carlo
  - resident state
  - CUDA
  - HIP
license: MIT
